        "original_id": "c807a091-4093-57c8-8dbc-7904ab4f3858",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Wesley, Charles Wesley, George Whitefield, Edward Perronet\n- Organizations: Church of England, Methodism\n- Concepts: Anglican clerics, 18th-century revival\n\nFacts:\n- Methodism originated as a revival within the 18th-century Church of England.\n- John Wesley was born on 28 June 1703 and was an English Anglican cleric and theologian.\n- John Wesley, Charles Wesley, and George Whitefield founded Methodism.\n- Edward Perronet was born in 1726 as the son of an Anglican priest.\n- Edward Perronet worked closely with Anglican priest John Wesley and his brother Charles Wesley for many years during England's 18th-century revival.\n- John Wesley died on 2 March 1791.\n- Methodism became a separate denomination after John Wesley's death.\n- Edward Perronet died on 2 January 1792.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
